    {
      "id": "claim_b5afd9cd3c5c496095782e977ee254d1",
      "statement": "TaskLogger.append is wrapped in a try/catch that silently absorbs database write failures, so a logger failure cannot break the surrounding task. TaskLogger.updateProgress and TaskLogger.updateStatus re-read the existing logs array from tasks, append a new entry, and persist it inside a single update, so concurrent appends can race only on the last entry.",
